#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Less Than (Or Equal To) Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fcaa68c-20d1-560a-80a4-8d8d524032ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fcaa68c-20d1-560a-80a4-8d8d524032ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292687} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd4924d-570a-559d-b2dc-f56e552f2ee0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d393db0e-75b4-5c46-834f-a74cc084b33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d393db0e-75b4-5c46-834f-a74cc084b33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292689} :answer-field/id #uuid "a01c1233-e863-5907-aa31-4700b542c890" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc99565c-080c-5c9b-96d1-0d0f950e06bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc99565c-080c-5c9b-96d1-0d0f950e06bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292691} :answer-field/id #uuid "49191652-8c7a-52ab-9393-0549495c3b5d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0311ef6-fe92-51b8-a43d-3cc837a8ac32" :question/math-academy-id "q-276402" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-8x<0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-8x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =0 \\\\ x(x-8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=8,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/8c4acb1db29c8479f946d6d047fe79d9a87d7162de1ff0725e59052f93df85ce.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0<x<8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca4696f2-7f99-5bb5-a2e6-2f896009a3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{3}{2}]\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292694} {:answer/id #uuid "b39057be-c22a-538e-b6d8-b817efa2b994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292695} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb63f72-c77c-597e-a6e6-7af09edbaf8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292696} {:answer/id #uuid "3b55f7bb-d26d-55e3-b17f-7c1623a1c745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292697} {:answer/id #uuid "9447c28b-d9a2-5fcb-8884-1bc8b89ca063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b55f7bb-d26d-55e3-b17f-7c1623a1c745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6edfb28-dc7c-5965-a229-4e405703ffe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d17d341f-d303-5767-85ec-0a66ef9ec1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-276407" :question/problem "Find the solution of $x+3\\ge 2{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\ge 2{x}^{2} \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+x+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}+x+3$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}+x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-3 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-3x)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ x(2x-3)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)(x-\\frac{3}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/86d7fbea75961bdb83c014ca9febb735e6a1745f71e8e094de416998b2072630.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+x+3\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Quadratic “Or Equal To” Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894b802a-63f9-5a6a-bcd2-d93dcfbcdff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "894b802a-63f9-5a6a-bcd2-d93dcfbcdff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292701} :answer-field/id #uuid "8572a649-145f-5e57-850c-73e70d41aafb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aea1369d-d4c7-5774-96ed-e33aece856fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea1369d-d4c7-5774-96ed-e33aece856fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292703} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9e19c9-79f3-5995-9c26-a1b6ff4d3e07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3f622fb-d8a5-5f8e-a1ab-925800ff1e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-276408" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}\\le 12x$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & \\le 12x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-12x & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-12x$ lies **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/d81805f304bd45ddd595bd251202226d2b1ced494fe7816d0bc9f17ee8f998a0.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,3].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8328ccbf-79c0-5bcc-b61d-5122d411fdb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞, 2)∪(8, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183144} {:answer/id #uuid "89a966b8-328b-5bbf-b87b-11ca757f14d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-4, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183145} {:answer/id #uuid "9c210885-81c8-5ab5-b586-a269305add27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞,-2)∪(4, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183146} {:answer/id #uuid "1218fd9b-7c15-586e-97f2-6f4f1efaaa41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183147} {:answer/id #uuid "6607bb49-1824-58cf-80ff-93d98746d6d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (2, 8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1218fd9b-7c15-586e-97f2-6f4f1efaaa41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (-2, 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183147} :answer-field/id #uuid "8793b6ae-0734-5a4d-96ee-0d5a7c4ac1ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b253cbb-e3d2-5ab6-bf1c-b7d0c090be37" :question/math-academy-id "q-3859" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-2x<8.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & <8 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-2x-8$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/83e87f616c1e9a74065016df2d6a0bbfac5bcdc8ee9326721b13a2bd8a8f16d4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8<0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Strict Quadratic Inequalities That Require Rearrangement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1f4781f-9aad-5beb-af91-cfc8ad57f970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2} < x < 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183156} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdee864-62d1-5bf4-b565-7ee9b0dc36fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2} < x < 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183157} {:answer/id #uuid "e426b6f4-0994-5fa4-a794-eff926789ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x < 0$ or $x > 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183158} {:answer/id #uuid "42301df3-4534-52e7-8564-bdfa2522e1fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 < x < \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183159} {:answer/id #uuid "7169f734-fc2b-5d9f-9a41-8ebb7eb9ae0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x < - \\frac{1}{2}$ or $x > 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42301df3-4534-52e7-8564-bdfa2522e1fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 < x < \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183159} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5fb79a-a308-588a-ac43-4e489cd5bcb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1459c427-2f65-5af9-93bd-226984ba8bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-3952" :question/problem "Find the solution of $-6{x}^{2}>-3x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2} & >-3x \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+3x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-6{x}^{2}+3x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -3x(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/3dff64c74abd4981c69686cbbf7d79fdd49c7a7fde3bb266b2b6e11c441bcf20.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-6{x}^{2}+3x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$"}]}
